<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:56:01Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Spain's Sanchez says no 'solid proof' that Morocco planned Ceuta crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd5822318cffa42dcd37b048923961e42b9504cf98ef1323ee4a489908ce72fe</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T11:58:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-spain-s-sanchez-says-no-solid-proof-that-morocco-planned-ceuta-crisis" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez has told lawmakers that there is no evidence the Ceuta migrant crisis was orchestrated by Morocco's government. His remarks come a day after tens of thousands of people took part in protests across the country to criticize his handling of the migrant influx. He acknowledged that Ceuta was both a humanitarian crisis and an administrative challenge. But he rejected the findings of a police report that seemed to lay blame on Morocco. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid, Spain.</summary></entry><entry><title>Meloni government sets longevity record in Italy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:573aef53bfbf463a581db149c9b97ff2c1af5e0bd5c78171db71cd78fe6e4e19</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:55:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T10:11:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-meloni-government-sets-longevity-record-in-italy--a69c834200f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-meloni-government-sets-longevity-record-in-italy" /><summary type="html">Giorgia Meloni's hard-right government has been in power for 1,413 days. She surpassed the record set by Silvio Berlusconi between 2001 and 2005, making her government Italy's longest serving uninterrupted government since World War II, after a period of intense instability. Italy has had 68 governments in the last 80 years. Giorgia Meloni and her party will celebrate the feat on Friday with a huge pre-election rally in the southern city of Bari. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta tells more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Norway seizes Russian ship to enforce $4.22 billion Ukrainian compensation claim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8de1cfb5bd71c7c063d6fd00501092792d97ea08423f07d806e10300d186ff3b</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T10:07:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-norway-seizes-russian-ship-to-enforce-4-22-billion-ukrainian-arbitration-claim" /><summary type="html">Norway said Wednesday it had seized a Russian ship as part of a Ukrainian effort to recover $4.22 billion awarded to state energy firm Naftogaz over Russia’s seizure of its assets in Crimea in 2014. The Professor Molchanov vessel was detained off the Arctic Svalbard archipelago after a Norwegian court ordered its arrest.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>No 'solid proof' Morocco planned Ceuta migrant rush, says Spanish PM Sanchez</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4506e0cfcfc145ffa203a75d0136b62ec35906e2bbf4894f550e384841fc58c</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:55:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T08:18:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-no-solid-proof-morocco-planned-ceuta-migrant-rush--1ed53eaa7182.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-spanish-pm-sanchez-says-no-solid-proof-morocco-planned-ceuta-migrant-rush" /><summary type="html">Spanish Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez said Thursday there was no "solid proof" that Morocco orchestrated a migrant rush into Ceuta in July following the emergence of a police report highlighting multiple failings by Moroccan security forces.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Churchillian moment? Macron in Britain amid scramble to boost European defence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5e78927f35dd29855c5a4ccba877cdd2212c93728fcea41a3b32114efd474ce</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:55:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T07:39:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260903-churchillian-moment-macron-in-britain-amid-scramble-to-boost-european-defence--13e2ba2d0940.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260903-churchillian-moment-macron-in-britain-amid-scramble-to-boost-european-defence" /><summary type="html">What can an 11th-century comic strip about the Norman Conquest of England tell us about the spectre of sea change in 2026 Europe? France’s president is on hand for the hottest ticket in London, the first-ever cross-Channel visit of the Bayeux Tapestry, which, for the record, is not a tapestry but a delicate scroll of embroidered cloth that chronicles a radical turning point in our continent’s history. Should France’s outgoing president and the British monarch who welcomes him be likened more to the defending Saxons or the invading Normans?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Macron, Burnham hold talks on migrants, EU after viewing Bayeux Tapestry in London</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8800662b11ba2292ed6dc5af8ffc5e805eefbefc801986d375190c321cca447</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:55:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T06:47:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-macron-to-hold-first-talks-with-uk-s-burnham-after-viewing-bayeux-tapestry-in-london--cf8928d0a830.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260903-macron-to-hold-first-talks-with-uk-s-burnham-after-viewing-bayeux-tapestry-in-london" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron and UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham held their first talks on Thursday after meeting a day earlier at the Bayeux Tapestry exhibition at the British Museum. Topping the agenda were several issues, including migrant boats crossing the Channel, British-EU relations and the Ukraine war.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine warns Russian airspace ‘not safe’ in message to UN aviation watchdog</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4519979547313b260718ce7b89f9278a5661d010088033182dd8fade09878402</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:55:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T22:46:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-un-civilian-flight-safety-russian-airspace-ukraine--07f316548901.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-un-civilian-flight-safety-russian-airspace-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Ukraine urged the UN aviation agency to call for a full ban on flights through Russian airspace after President Volodymyr Zelensky warned it was becoming unsafe. Kyiv plans increased retaliation against intensified Russian strikes but would target only military facilities, Zelensky said, citing growing Ukrainian drone activity over Russia.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Outrage in Malta as court acquits tycoon in investigative journalist murder case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7d700a76213e3f2d700d6ddb52195ab03d27c2ca79f174e79149c2bdaad3e6b</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:55:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T21:56:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-reporter-murder--2cac186cd75a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-reporter-murder" /><summary type="html">A Maltese court on Wednesday acquitted tycoon Yorgen Fenech of orchestrating the 2017 car-bomb killing of investigative journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia, a verdict that drew condemnation from her family and press freedom advocates. Her family said the acquittal denied Caruana Galizia justice, while her son called it a “terrible decision”.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky warns airlines Russian skies not safe due to Ukraine drones</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:62c04fe5e6ff0a077cd2d96d7c4650193c1ffcfe9600e93f4dc2daa2ed73b4ba</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:56:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T19:32:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/zelensky-warns-airlines-russian-skies-not-safe-due-to-ukraine-drones--0846dc6a9c24.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/zelensky-warns-airlines-russian-skies-not-safe-due-to-ukraine-drones" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky warned Tuesday that his country's drones would make Russia's airspace "completely unsafe" for the duration of the war, drawing accusations of "state terrorism" from Russian leader Vladimir Putin. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Former British Military Intelligence Officer Philip Ingram explains that Zelensky's warning is addressed to "those international airlines from the Middle East, from South East Asia, China included that are still operating into Moscow" adding that "it's all part of the information war and bringing the overall conflict to the Russian people".</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia blamed for explosive-laden drone found at German airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4961ee2a90494728aef9df5541a0b52e96a4ba3a2a8816d65e0fed6684f02d1b</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T16:11:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-russia-blamed-for-explosive-laden-drone-found-at-german-airport--a786ed42be94.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-russia-blamed-for-explosive-laden-drone-found-at-german-airport" /><summary type="html">After #Germany blamed #Russia for the explosive-laden #drone found at #Leipzig airport on August 4, #Berlin has introduced new sanctions against #Moscow. Namely, its consulate in #Bonn and the Russian House - a cultural centre thought to be a Russian #spy hub - in #Berlin.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany investigates suspected power substation sabotage, Russia summons German envoy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9e9c27bc2067b39733179cfb530b47815b396bda546993e7d9e0339db042dff</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T13:15:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-germany-ivestigates-suspected-power-substation-sabotage-russia-summons-german-envoy--4853f0a31700.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-germany-ivestigates-suspected-power-substation-sabotage-russia-summons-german-envoy" /><summary type="html">Two incidents that disrupted power distribution systems in Germany are being investigated for sabotage, authorities said Wednesday, while one of them was also being examined for possible terrorism links. Meanwhile Russia said it was summoning Germany's charge d'affaires after Berlin blamed Moscow for last month's attempted drone attack at Leipzig airport.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Drone incident in Germany has ‘hallmarks of state-sponsored terrorism’, EU's Kallas says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:981e71fc3119369219c8f309505c0cb2d1e0a5206abeaf444148f6270550653b</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T12:59:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-eu-summons-russia-envoys-eyes-sanctions-after-germany-drone-attack--5007b80aa030.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-eu-summons-russia-envoys-eyes-sanctions-after-germany-drone-attack" /><summary type="html">Last month's incident involving an explosive-laden drone at Leipzig airport bears "all the hallmarks of state-sponsored terrorism," EU foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas said Wednesday. Germany has blamed Russia for the "hybrid attack". The EU has summoned the Russian envoy, and member states were doing the same, Kallas said.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Macron urges France, UK to forge closer bond as Bayeux Tapestry goes on display in Britain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b50f2bbd40e8130820b73e714d24aae5c8f850745b8a095697a4c5f7a2384779</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T01:27:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-france-s-macron-in-britain-to-help-unveil-bayeux-tapestry--e5685b353904.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260902-france-s-macron-in-britain-to-help-unveil-bayeux-tapestry" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron called on France and Britain to forge closer ties on Wednesday as he joined King Charles III and Prime Minister Andy Burnham to mark the historic loan of the Bayeux Tapestry to the British Museum. Macron said the two allies could build a bond “as close as the threads” of the 950-year-old artwork, which depicts the Norman conquest of England.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Germany blames Russia for airport drone incident, hits back with sanctions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17036af734cd82b66b708c51f164f55e9f7a74997948f41262524f6b03dc590d</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T20:58:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/germany-blames-russia-for-airport-drone-incident-hits-back-with-sanctions--4fb45ecf7b0d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/germany-blames-russia-for-airport-drone-incident-hits-back-with-sanctions" /><summary type="html">Germany on Tuesday blamed Russia for an attempted "hybrid attack" involving an explosive-laden drone at a strategic airport last month and announced diplomatic counter-measures. The European Union expressed "full solidarity" with Germany, NATO assured that it would defend its members and countries including Britain, Estonia and Poland offered strong backing. Germany will close Russia's consulate in the former capital Bonn later this month, and cancel the contract for the Russian House, a cultural centre in Berlin, said Foreign Minister Johann Wadephul. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Burnham pledges to restore hope as he makes his House of Commons debut as UK leader</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4038f29dc0d6bdbc82d2d50eecc485b31bce89d29d5964fd70e542fd37e9fe1</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T20:54:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/burnham-pledges-to-restore-hope-as-he-makes-his-house-of-commons-debut-as-uk-leader--37fef2f9fef3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/burnham-pledges-to-restore-hope-as-he-makes-his-house-of-commons-debut-as-uk-leader" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Andy Burnham faced lawmakers in the House of Commons on Tuesday for the first time since becoming U.K. leader six weeks ago, with wars in Europe and the Middle East weighing on his promise to kick-start the economy, ease the cost of living and oversee a radical redistribution of power from London to Britain's regions. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Dr Martin Farr, Senior Lecturer in British Contemporary History at Newcastle University.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany blames Russia for Leipzig airport drone attack, orders Russian consulate closed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f303657f98dc811fbc6a7b0dea93f19a0256d6b71f5970ca99ef5ff09bdd094e</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T17:00:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-germany-blames-russia-for-leipzig-airport-drone-attack-orders-russian-consulate-closed--4237b34f641e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-germany-blames-russia-for-leipzig-airport-drone-attack-orders-russian-consulate-closed" /><summary type="html">Germany's government on Tuesday blamed Russia for an attempted attack at Leipzig/Halle Airport on 4 August using an explosive-laden drone, and announced that it would shut down a Russian consulate among other measures against Moscow. French ​President Emmanuel Macron ​said he supported the ​adoption ‌of ⁠new European sanctions ‌against Russia after the attempted drone attack.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>What to know about the new UK PM's agenda as he faces lawmakers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c63a1a02c42074197b9eedb6a9e21662c6ce70d182a4342e57c4848d8e4c2e8</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T15:39:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-new-uk-pm-s-agenda-as-he-faces-lawmakers--7159b8695669.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-new-uk-pm-s-agenda-as-he-faces-lawmakers" /><summary type="html">Since taking office on July 20, Burnham has traveled around the country promising to deliver renewed national optimism after the downbeat two-year tenure of his predecessor Keir Starmer. Now, it's time for him to face lawmakers for the first time since he has taken office after an unusually long time without having to do so due to the summer recess. FRANCE 24's Benedicte Paviot tells us what to know from his speech.</summary></entry><entry><title>Replay: UK PM Andy Burnham faces lawmakers for first time since taking office</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e8a000ae8829102ea4f976e5f24b03b8ce4d5ea6268bbc850adc2214b5f1b84</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T15:22:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/replay-uk-pm-andy-burnham-faces-lawmakers-for-first-time-since-taking-office--b2983eb40ac0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/replay-uk-pm-andy-burnham-faces-lawmakers-for-first-time-since-taking-office" /><summary type="html">Rewatch UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham's first speech to parliament since taking office six weeks prior.</summary></entry><entry><title>After 'unprecedented honeymoon', UK PM faces lawmakers for first time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82c4bb37a70692a3ec829330a908f6ddff93e7fb65835278fdaa5323368f44a4</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T15:10:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/after-unprecedented-honeymoon-uk-pm-faces-lawmakers-for-first-time--5c153c598613.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/after-unprecedented-honeymoon-uk-pm-faces-lawmakers-for-first-time" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Andy Burnham will face lawmakers in the House of Commons on September 1 for the first time since becoming UK leader six weeks ago. This comes as the wars in Europe and the Middle East weighing on his promise to kick-start the economy and ease the cost of living. Andy Burnham has enjoyed quite a long time without facing lawmakers due to the summer recess. FRANCE 24's Benedicte Paviot tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>At least 12 killed and over a dozen injured in Russian strikes on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f69165273b81801b118a1ac8b95aa96c3a95ef246dd515b46bd468c7cec9e59</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T14:56:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/at-least-12-killed-and-over-a-dozen-injured-in-russian-strikes-on-kyiv--d546607aa696.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/at-least-12-killed-and-over-a-dozen-injured-in-russian-strikes-on-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Russian air attacks killed 12 people and injured many more in Kyiv and the surrounding region early on September 1, authorities said, marking the sixth straight day of intense strikes on the Ukrainian capital. Those injured three children, just as Ukrainian pupils return to school. In a new tactic, Moscow has sent swarms of new jet-powered drones to ⁠plague Kyiv and nearby areas day and night, killing residents and damaging homes and warehouses.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia's G20 US invitation severely criticised by European countries</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4f45c22f6d780db5f0ec2ebda6858b1c7ec9fe8559b8f5bdd906ced27b4e98f</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:48:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-s-g20-us-invitation-severely-criticised-by-european-countries--bc062679808d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-s-g20-us-invitation-severely-criticised-by-european-countries" /><summary type="html">Finance ministers and central bank governors from the group of 20 major economies are meeting for two days in Asheville, North Carolina. With the United States holding the rotating G20 presidency, Washington is trying to rally partners towards greater economic pressure on Iran and find ways to boost growth. But an unexpected attendee drew fierce criticism.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine hopes for bolstered support as EU defence ministers meet in Dublin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a618ffffcd901d7e2cd57099e78fddde54d47e024ade46a92d9109eb801e6de5</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:34:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-hopes-for-bolstered-support-as-eu-defence-ministers-meet-in-dublin--524abd2c9af0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-hopes-for-bolstered-support-as-eu-defence-ministers-meet-in-dublin" /><summary type="html">EU defence ministers grapple with bolstering Ukraine's air defences, as worries grow over Russia's campaign to destabilise Kyiv's European backers. This comes as Moscow is taking advantage of Kyiv running low on US-built air defence missiles to intensify its attacks on the country. EU ministers are also expected to discuss Russia's hybrid war against Ukraine's European allies. FRANCE 24's Angela Diffley tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK needs 'substantial change', says PM Andy Burnham in maiden parliament speech</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ff7d7a6f256ad3d28385a2e99457743260d2461b00dd9365fc3d8f3f6339e56</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:21:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-live-uk-pm-andy-burnham-faces-mps-for-first-time-since-taking-office--eb38aa025937.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-live-uk-pm-andy-burnham-faces-mps-for-first-time-since-taking-office" /><summary type="html">The United Kingdom's new Prime Minister Andy Burnham said the UK needed "substantial change" at his maiden speech in the House of Commons on Tuesday. Burnham has promised to deliver renewed national optimism after the downbeat two-year tenure of predecessor Keir Starmer, who announced Tuesday that he would resign his seat in Parliament after 11 years.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Massive' Russian missile, drone attacks on Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58b7d03e39c6f2e477512e4fc273b47f82ca017a9574f06cac66dca1f6b12d3a</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:50:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-massive-russian-missile-drone-attacks-on-kyiv--2741b6e31ce0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260901-massive-russian-missile-drone-attacks-on-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Russian air attacks killed 12 people and injured several more in Kyiv early on Tuesday, authorities said, in the sixth consecutive day of strikes on the Ukrainian capital. Russia, which began its full-scale invasion of its smaller neighbour in 2022, has escalated its air attacks in recent months, as gains made on the ground have slowed.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia fired over 2,800 drones at Ukraine in August amid war tactic change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ec635ee548df2136265470ce305e4463a71a05f5806203c5c435af96021e960</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:49:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-fired-over-2-800-drones-at-ukraine-in-august-amid-war-tactic-change--64c40c91d843.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-fired-over-2-800-drones-at-ukraine-in-august-amid-war-tactic-change" /><summary type="html">Over the course of the month of August, Russia launched more than 2,800 jet-propelled drones at Ukraine, a type of drone that is harder to shoot down. That has come with a massive uptick in the number of drones used, considerind those now found on the frontline are quite a new model: Ukrainian authorities say they are pressed into service almost immediately after leaving the factory. FRANCE 24's Oliver Farry looks at those new drones, and how Russia is using them to try and change the course of the war.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia targets Kyiv and its region for sixth consecutive night of attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1efa3912babea288686f0bedeaacbcabc83f0dde0536af79bb64ad0beeb0efd1</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:39:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-targets-kyiv-and-its-region-for-sixth-consecutive-night-of-attacks--4b2d5a3bbbf0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-targets-kyiv-and-its-region-for-sixth-consecutive-night-of-attacks" /><summary type="html">At least nine people have been killed and 14 injured in Russian strikes on Ukraine overnight. Moscow targeted Kyiv and the wider region in the attack, hitting a railway depot in the Kyiv. Russia's defence ministry said it had also struck infrastructure in the Southern Odesa region. Russia has intensified strikes on the beleaguered Ukrainian cities in recent weeks disrupting the daily lives of millions of people and triggering up to a dozen air-raid alerts a day.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lake Annecy gun linked to unsolved 2012 murder of British family in French Alps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:127462655798b2ff5ca67ba132b7798222d69e50876376b70679f49e8bd6110b</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T08:21:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-lake-annecy-gun-linked-to-unsolved-2012-murder-british-iraqi-family-french-alps-chevaline--d65d925f5927.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-lake-annecy-gun-linked-to-unsolved-2012-murder-british-iraqi-family-french-alps-chevaline" /><summary type="html">French officials say a Luger pistol fished out from the bottom of Lake Annecy shows similarities to the weapon used in the notorious 2012 killings of a British-Iraqi family and a French cyclist in the nearby village of Chevaline, opening up a new lead in a case that has befuddled investigators for over a decade.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Safe days in Russian skies are over,' warns Zelensky</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ec7e2d60fe9687bb5cd0aac09778d5b005685d2ff43f1cf997ad37cd79cdcd9</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T06:04:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-live-deadly-russian-air-attack-hits-railway-depot-in-kyiv--abb7e72e6993.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-live-deadly-russian-air-attack-hits-railway-depot-in-kyiv" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky on Tuesday warned airlines, insurance firms and passengers that Russian airspace would be "completely unsafe" and filled with Ukrainian drones for the duration of the war. His address came after a night of relentless Russian bombardment in Ukraine, which killed at least a dozen people. Read our liveblog to see how all the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian missile and drone attack on Kyiv kills at least eight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e271ed8a0cba6b4d6b248c4f3810617079e79296fdd016f5ce0036f82c52153</id><updated>2026-09-03T12:53:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T02:26:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-russian-missile-and-drone-attack-on-kyiv-kills-at-least-four--dac5ac77b624.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260901-russian-missile-and-drone-attack-on-kyiv-kills-at-least-four" /><summary type="html">A massive Russian missile and drone attack on Kyiv and its surrounding region killed at least eight people and wounded more than a dozen overnight, Ukrainian officials said Tuesday, as children prepared to return to school amid heightened fears of further strikes.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
